Full test suite passes with no failures.

**Root cause:** The deprecated `Week(Date time, TimeZone zone)` constructor ignored its `zone` parameter and always delegated using `RegularTimePeriod.DEFAULT_TIME_ZONE` instead of the passed-in `zone`, so the week-of-year was computed relative to the wrong time zone whenever the caller's zone differed from the default.

**Fix:** In `source/org/jfree/data/time/Week.java`, changed the constructor to delegate with the actual `zone` argument instead of the hardcoded default:
```java
public Week(Date time, TimeZone zone) {
    this(time, zone, Locale.getDefault());
}
```
